<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Africa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> is the eastern region of the African continent, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> coast. It was home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a> and a target of colonial expansion by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>. Its ports were also reached by Chinese trade and diplomacy in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a>, notably by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he">Zheng He</a>'s voyages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-africa.jpg" alt="East Africa" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daljir · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_East_Africa_Countries.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
